    "lawCode": "Amd §95, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Public Officers Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S3020\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the public officers law, in relation to records\nrequested through electronic mail\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF THE BILL :\nThe purpose of this bill is to require agencies to accept and respond\nto requests for records under the Personal Privacy Protection Law.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nThis bill would require each agency, when responding to requests for\nrecords under the Personal Privacy Protection Law, to accept records\nrequest submitted through electronic mail if such agency has\nreasonable means available. It also requires the agency to respond to\nsuch requests by electronic mail, wherever possible using form\nconsistent with the forms developed by the Committee on Open\nGovernment.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nLast year, the Freedom of Information Law was amended to require that\nagencies transmit requested records via electronic mail when they have\nthe ability to do so.  This bill would extend this provision to the\nrelated Personal Privacy Protection Law, which allows individuals who\nhave data kept about them by New York State agencies to request copies\nof that information from the State. Legislation such as this helps\nincrease the transparency and accountability of state agencies and\nfurther empowers individual citizens to control and monitor how their\ngovernment operates.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nThis is a new bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
